                    "message": "inventory item PDI has this description\n\n```\ndescription: >\n    Implement to provide basic item attributes.  Required by all objects within\n    the inventory namespace.\n```\n\nso i assume we must have the interface `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item`\n\nbut we can also have `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Fan` interface on top of that.\n\nWhat do you think \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe Inventory.Item.Fan counts as an Inventory.Item due to interface hierarchy, but I am currently struggling to find anything explicitly stating that in plain English :p \n\nThe PDI links I included in my other reply should shed light on my thinking here, at least..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Fan` does not have such properties, they are on inventory item interface"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "My current understanding is that Inventory.Item.Fan interface inherits the properties called out in the Inventory.Item interface\n\nI *think* that's why Item.Fan has no properties specified, just an association stanza\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Fan.interface.yaml\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item.interface.yaml"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Looked at `build/gen/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Fan/client.hpp`\n\nand there is no include of any inventory item headers.\n\nSo i am not sure if it inherits those. Also did not find any properties there.\n\nIf it's supposed to be inheriting then the PDI is probably broken there.\n\nAre there any users like bmcweb out there directly reading properties from the fan inventory item?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "You would just add the 2 interfaces separately on the same object path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/TachSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Oh, that's good info. I'll update accordingly."
                }
            ],
